7592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415060 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415060 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186415056 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415060 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f0e50222-5322-5dc6-95c0-87aed25c41a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415061 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415060 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415061 #edb/ref 1069 "q-35580" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415061 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415061 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly dependent and ${{v}_{1},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$\n- ${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$\n- ${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415061 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c07b7ca-2c8b-5a74-a857-c6a369e5fb28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415061 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent set, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas a non-zero solution.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, solving equation ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ for ${v}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=-\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{x}_{3}}{{x}_{2}}{v}_{3}-\\frac{{x}_{4}}{{x}_{2}}{v}_{4}.\n$$\n\nMoreover, ${x}_{2}$ can't be zero because then\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nwill have a non-zero solution and that's a contradiction as ${{v}_{1},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent.\nHence, ${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the set ${{v}_{1},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent set, the equation \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{3}+{x}_{3}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas no non-zero solution. Hence, ${v}_{4}$ is not a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415062 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415063 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415062 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "194a201e-a484-52b1-85fa-bf0a3ff539e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415062 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415063 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415063 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "390603f7-3592-5dc2-9f55-cc90d76600ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415063 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186329740 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415064 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415064 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "413d02a4-dfef-5bc6-b884-f744f0683a08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415064 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415065 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bca21e33-420e-51ea-b2c1-ea2ef421580a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415065 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415066 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415066 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ccfee361-efb3-56f5-ae8f-8f48353bd1c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415066 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186243998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420706 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420714 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420706 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420706 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420706 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420706 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420706 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420706 #edb/ref 1045 "Linear Independence in Abstract Vector Spaces" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420706 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186420718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420706 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420706 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420706 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "86f80e75-0963-5bd9-910a-02c8b66996e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420707 #edb/ref 1080 "The set is linearly independent" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420707 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420707 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "19ddf127-9fb5-5724-b669-1d5d25a58040" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420708 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{4}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420708 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420708 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "37daef1d-9729-5a8c-96e9-3c9478596dc7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420709 #edb/ref 1080 "-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420709 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420709 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "561c2f0d-be65-5b74-80cb-c4d610f62978" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420710 #edb/ref 1080 "7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420710 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420710 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7107938f-dc39-590b-a878-c6a64a6afe0b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420711 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{7}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420711 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420711 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7e6ca647-3da8-59df-a01b-f1f1276bf3fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420712 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420712 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420712 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420712 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420710 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420712 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420712 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420712 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420712 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420712 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f41fca13-4375-5dd3-80b4-d2dbcf42196f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420713 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420712 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420713 #edb/ref 1069 "q-35759" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420713 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420713 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the set of matrices ${A,B,C},$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 20 & -12\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -7 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nIf the set is linearly dependent, find the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}$ from a non-zero solution of ${x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O,$ where $O$ is the $2\\times 2$ zero-matrix." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420713 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0b9ee9fe-348f-5bee-8c67-e9425237ec58" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420713 #edb/ref 1074 "If the set is linearly dependent, then there exist ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ not all zero such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O.\n$$\n\nOtherwise, if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ the set is linearly independent.\n\nSubstituting the matrices $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 20 & -12\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -7 & -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & -5{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4{x}_{2} \\\\ 20{x}_{2} & -12{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3} & 5{x}_{3} \\\\ -7{x}_{3} & -5{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3} & -4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+20{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3} & -5{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+20{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the corresponding augmented matrix and reduce it to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 20 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -12 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+5{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 20 & -15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 15 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+5{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-3){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are  the $1$st,  $2$nd and $3$rd. Therefore, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 10{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich has only the zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\nConsequently, ${A,B,C}$ is linearly independent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420714 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420714 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "13861d32-2afe-51b5-bbef-cdba909877c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420714 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360491 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420715 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420715 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "26514834-a2cf-541c-940e-f1a92276ce78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420715 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186244004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420716 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420714 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420716 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "91898925-eff3-5fa3-8a62-f041326f9f41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420716 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186420713 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420717 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9a3eaaac-6a96-5a5c-a458-0780e627e72a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420717 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186244008 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420718 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420718 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a04781cc-ebc3-5bc2-92d1-20e2247f29f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420718 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415061 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
